-fix.stdout.log:57:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":2,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"{\\\"file_path\\\": \\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.\"}},\"session_id\":\"ceae9c6b-d571-491c-ba4d-0d8e5cb3a7be\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"e7bda88f-1105-4e1f-b506-24eefc5d1dbe\"}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/004-quick-fix.stdout.log:58:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":2,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"ts\"}},\"session_id\":\"ceae9c6b-d571-491c-ba4d-0d8e5cb3a7be\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"6f8b2ad8-154a-4a82-811c-fa5677cc283c\"}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/004-quick-fix.stdout.log:59:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_013zjUhudUGuyZP3Ehy2yaUg\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Story 4: Lifecycle Exercise\\n2\\t\\n3\\t### Summary\\n4\\t<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\n5\\tAdd the full-surface lifecycle exercise in PI-extension call order across SDK, replay, teardown, and CLI parity legs.\\n6\\t\\n7\\t### Description\\n8\\t<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\n9\\t**User Profile:** The future PI extension calls the SDK surfaces in the sequence this exercise rehearses; the operator uses CLI reads at checkpoints.\\n10\\t\\n11\\t**Objective:** Exercise every built v1 surface through one deterministic sequence and verify contract coherence across epics.\\n12\\t\\n13\\t**Scope In:** Scripted sequence: create thread → intake multi-turn tool-heavy batches → background drain settles → status → compact (profile) → pull → inspect (overview, view, health) → edit + delete → rebuild drains → health confirms → second compact → pull → materialize.\\n14\\t\\n15\\t**Scope Out:** This story does not prove real-inference readiness. No real network or real-provider call is allowed. Quality review of deterministic-provider output remains outside this epic.\\n16\\t\\n17\\t**Dependencies:** Stories 1-3 complete; Epic 03 complete.\\n18\\t\\n19\\t### Acceptance Criteria\\n20\\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\n21\\t- **AC-5.1**: The full sequence completes through one real SDK configuration with the deterministic provider: every operation returns ok, zero network, zero real-provider calls.\\n22\\t\\n23\\t- **AC-5.2**: Checkpoint coherence: post-compact pull serves bands + tail; post-mutation health shows the cleared set pending; post-drain health shows it ready; the second compact's view reflects post-edit content; the second compact receipt's sweep section agrees with the health report taken immediately before it.\\n24\\t\\n25\\t- **TC-5.1** (AC-5.1, AC-5.2): Scripted lifecycle with checkpoint assertions at each named step; receipt-vs-health cross-check exact.\\n26\\t\\n27\\t- **AC-5.3**: End-to-end determinism: the whole sequence replayed on a fresh thread produces byte-identical pull outputs and materialized files.\\n28\\t\\n29\\t- **TC-5.2** (AC-5.3): Replay on a fresh thread → hash equality on every pull output and the materialized file.\\n30\\t\\n31\\t- **AC-5.4**: No in-memory dependency: tearing down the SDK instance between phases and continuing on a fresh `createSdk` yields the same end state as the uninterrupted run.\\n32\\t\\n33\\t- **TC-5.3** (AC-5.4): Teardown and recreate the SDK between intake/compact/mutation phases → final pull, health, and materialized file identical to TC-5.1's.\\n34\\t\\n35\\t- **AC-5.5**: Operator parity: inspect and view reads driven through the spawned CLI at checkpoints return the same JSON as the in-process SDK calls at those checkpoints.\\n36\\t\\n37\\t- **TC-5.4** (AC-5.5): Process-suite leg: spawned CLI inspect/view/messages reads at three checkpoints equal the in-process results.\\n38\\t\\n39\\t### Technical Design\\n40\\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\n41\\t#### Architecture Context\\n42\\t\\n43\\tThis story adds the shared lifecycle fixture and the full-surface verification legs. It introduces no production surface; it proves the built SDK and CLI surfaces work in PI-extension call order with deterministic provider setup only.\\n44\\t\\n45\\tThe lifecycle script names phases and returns results to tests. Assertions stay in tests so replay, teardown, and process legs drive the same sequence without re-describing it.\\n46\\t\\n47\\t#### Build Strategy\\n48\\t\\n49\\tStrategy: full-staged-risk\\n50\\t\\n51\\tReason:\\n52\\t- The story coordinates all prior surfaces, persistence reopen behavior, deterministic replay, materialization, and spawned CLI checkpoints.\\n53\\t\\n54\\tRisk Reminders:\\n55\\t- This is a seam proof, not a real-inference gate.\\n56\\t- Teardown must create a fresh SDK between phase groups.\\n57\\t- Process suite must report `ran`; missing auth or process prerequisites must not silently skip.\\n58\\t\\n59\\t#### Implementation Targets\\n60\\t\\n61\\t| Area | Files / Modules |\\n62\\t|------|-----------------|\\n63\\t| Lifecycle helper | `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts` |\\n64\\t| Default lifecycle tests | `test/lifecycle.test.ts` |\\n65\\t| Process checkpoint tests | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` |\\n66\\t| Consumed SDK/CLI surfaces | `src/sdk.ts`, `src/cli/inspect.ts`, `src/cli/messages-read.ts` |\\n67\\t\\n68\\t#### Design References\\n69\\t\\n70\\t- [tech-design.md §Context](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:6), lines 6-10\\n71\\t- [tech-design.md §Flow 5: Lifecycle Exercise](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:147), lines 147-149\\n72\\t- [tech-design.md §Testing Strategy](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:215), lines 215-217\\n73\\t- [tech-design.md §Work Breakdown](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:219), lines 219-230\\n74\\t- [test-plan.md §Test Files](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:6), lines 6-18\\n75\\t- [test-plan.md §TC → Test Mapping](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:20), lines 20-40\\n76\\t- [test-plan.md §Architecture-Risk Tests](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:42), lines 42-50\\n77\\t- [test-plan.md §Suite Accounting](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:52), lines 52-54\\n78\\t- [test-plan.md §Verification](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:66), lines 66-68\\n79\\t\\n80\\t#### Test Mapping\\n81\\t\\n82\\t| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\\n83\\t|----|-------------------|------------------|\\n84\\t| TC-5.1 | `test/lifecycle.test.ts :: full sequence + checkpoints` | Every phase returns ok; pull/health/compact/materialize checkpoints agree field-for-field where required. |\\n85\\t| TC-5.2 | `test/lifecycle.test.ts :: replay determinism` | Fresh-thread replay produces hash-equal pull outputs and materialized file. |\\n86\\t| TC-5.3 | `test/lifecycle.test.ts :: teardown continuity` | Fresh SDK between phase groups yields final pull, health, and materialized file equal to uninterrupted run. |\\n87\\t| TC-5.4 | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts :: checkpoint parity` | Spawned CLI overview/view/list reads at checkpoints deep-equal in-process SDK results. |\\n88\\t\\n89\\t#### Architecture-Risk Tests\\n90\\t\\n91\\t| Risk | Test File / Check | Test Description | Why AC/TC Mapping Alone Would Miss It |\\n92\\t|------|-------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------|\\n93\\t| Cross-epic lifecycle order drift | `test/lifecycle.test.ts` named-phase checkpoints | Run create, intake, drain, status, compact, pull, inspect, mutate, rebuild, compact, pull, materialize in order. | Individual story tests cannot catch ordering mismatches between surfaces. |\\n94\\t| Persistence relies on memory | `test/lifecycle.test.ts` fresh-SDK hook | Recreate SDK between phase groups and compare final outputs. | In-process success can hide state stored only in runtime memory. |\\n95\\t| CLI production path drift | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` process checkpoint leg | Spawn real commands and compare JSON to SDK checkpoints. | SDK tests do not prove command registration, stdout, or argv mapping. |\\n96\\t\\n97\\t#### Technical Notes\\n98\\t\\n99\\t- `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts` owns the sequence and phase names; tests own assertions.\\n100\\t- The receipt-vs-health check compares the second compact receipt sweep section with the health snapshot taken immediately before compact.\\n101\\t- Quality review of deterministic-provider text remains outside this epic.\\n102\\t\\n103\\t#### Anti-Shim Requirements\\n104\\t\\n105\\t- Use the real SDK configuration with deterministic provider and zero network/real-provider calls.\\n106\\t- Use real fresh SDK construction for teardown continuity.\\n107\\t- Use spawned CLI commands for checkpoint parity; do not call CLI handlers directly.\\n108\\t\\n109\\t#### Production Path Proof\\n110\\t\\n111\\t- Entrypoint: SDK surfaces from Epics 01-04 and spawned `lhc` commands.\\n112\\t- Registration/default path: the helper drives public SDK operations; process leg drives registered CLI commands.\\n113\\t- Evidence: lifecycle default tests, teardown continuity, replay determinism, and process checkpoint parity.\\n114\\t\\n115\\t#### Verification\\n116\\t\\n117\\t- Targeted: `pnpm verify`\\n118\\t- Story gate: `pnpm verify`\\n119\\t- Epic/process gate: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`\\n120\\t\\n121\\t#### Spec Deviations\\n122\\t\\n123\\tNone.\\n124\\t\\n125\\t### Definition of Done\\n126\\t<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n127\\t- The scripted lifecycle runs through one SDK configuration with deterministic provider only.\\n128\\t- Checkpoint assertions cover pull, health, compact receipt, rebuild, and materialized output.\\n129\\t- Replay on a fresh thread produces byte-identical pull outputs and materialized files.\\n130\\t- SDK teardown between phases produces the same final state as uninterrupted execution.\\n131\\t- Spawned CLI checkpoint reads match in-process SDK JSON.\\n132\\t- TC-5.1 through TC-5.4 pass with one primary owner in this story.\\n133\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"ceae9c6b-d571-491c-ba4d-0d8e5cb3a7be\",\"uuid\":\"5712fade-5f9e-42ed-a646-9f5d371a4ffb\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T15:34:43.383Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md\",\"content\":\"# Story 4: Lifecycle Exercise\\n\\n### Summary\\n<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\nAdd the full-surface lifecycle exercise in PI-extension call order across SDK, replay, teardown, and CLI parity legs.\\n\\n### Description\\n<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\n**User Profile:** The future PI extension calls the SDK surfaces in the sequence this exercise rehearses; the operator uses CLI reads at checkpoints.\\n\\n**Objective:** Exercise every built v1 surface through one deterministic sequence and verify contract coherence across epics.\\n\\n**Scope In:** Scripted sequence: create thread → intake multi-turn tool-heavy batches → background drain settles → status → compact (profile) → pull → inspect (overview, view, health) → edit + delete → rebuild drains → health confirms → second compact → pull → materialize.\\n\\n**Scope Out:** This story does not prove real-inference readiness. No real network or real-provider call is allowed. Quality review of deterministic-provider output remains outside this epic.\\n\\n**Dependencies:** Stories 1-3 complete; Epic 03 complete.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\n- **AC-5.1**: The full sequence completes through one real SDK configuration with the deterministic provider: every operation returns ok, zero network, zero real-provider calls.\\n\\n- **AC-5.2**: Checkpoint coherence: post-compact pull serves bands + tail; post-mutation health shows the cleared set pending; post-drain health shows it ready; the second compact's view reflects post-edit content; the second compact receipt's sweep section agrees with the health report taken immediately before it.\\n\\n- **TC-5.1** (AC-5.1, AC-5.2): Scripted lifecycle with checkpoint assertions at each named step; receipt-vs-health cross-check exact.\\n\\n- **AC-5.3**: End-to-end determinism: the whole sequence replayed on a fresh thread produces byte-identical pull outputs and materialized files.\\n\\n- **TC-5.2** (AC-5.3): Replay on a fresh thread → hash equality on every pull output and the materialized file.\\n\\n- **AC-5.4**: No in-memory dependency: tearing down the SDK instance between phases and continuing on a fresh `createSdk` yields the same end state as the uninterrupted run.\\n\\n- **TC-5.3** (AC-5.4): Teardown and recreate the SDK between intake/compact/mutation phases → final pull, health, and materialized file identical to TC-5.1's.\\n\\n- **AC-5.5**: Operator parity: inspect and view reads driven through the spawned CLI at checkpoints return the same JSON as the in-process SDK calls at those checkpoints.\\n\\n- **TC-5.4** (AC-5.5): Process-suite leg: spawned CLI inspect/view/messages reads at three checkpoints equal the in-process results.\\n\\n### Technical Design\\n<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\n#### Architecture Context\\n\\nThis story adds the shared lifecycle fixture and the full-surface verification legs. It introduces no production surface; it proves the built SDK and CLI surfaces work in PI-extension call order with deterministic provider setup only.\\n\\nThe lifecycle script names phases and returns results to tests. Assertions stay in tests so replay, teardown, and process legs drive the same sequence without re-describing it.\\n\\n#### Build Strategy\\n\\nStrategy: full-staged-risk\\n\\nReason:\\n- The story coordinates all prior surfaces, persistence reopen behavior, deterministic replay, materialization, and spawned CLI checkpoints.\\n\\nRisk Reminders:\\n- This is a seam proof, not a real-inference gate.\\n- Teardown must create a fresh SDK between phase groups.\\n- Process suite must report `ran`; missing auth or process prerequisites must not silently skip.\\n\\n#### Implementation Targets\\n\\n| Area | Files / Modules |\\n|------|-----------------|\\n| Lifecycle helper | `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts` |\\n| Default lifecycle tests | `test/lifecycle.test.ts` |\\n| Process checkpoint tests | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` |\\n| Consumed SDK/CLI surfaces | `src/sdk.ts`, `src/cli/inspect.ts`, `src/cli/messages-read.ts` |\\n\\n#### Design References\\n\\n- [tech-design.md §Context](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:6), lines 6-10\\n- [tech-design.md §Flow 5: Lifecycle Exercise](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:147), lines 147-149\\n- [tech-design.md §Testing Strategy](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:215), lines 215-217\\n- [tech-design.md §Work Breakdown](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:219), lines 219-230\\n- [test-plan.md §Test Files](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:6), lines 6-18\\n- [test-plan.md §TC → Test Mapping](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:20), lines 20-40\\n- [test-plan.md §Architecture-Risk Tests](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:42), lines 42-50\\n- [test-plan.md §Suite Accounting](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:52), lines 52-54\\n- [test-plan.md §Verification](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:66), lines 66-68\\n\\n#### Test Mapping\\n\\n| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\\n|----|-------------------|------------------|\\n| TC-5.1 | `test/lifecycle.test.ts :: full sequence + checkpoints` | Every phase returns ok; pull/health/compact/materialize checkpoints agree field-for-field where required. |\\n| TC-5.2 | `test/lifecycle.test.ts :: replay determinism` | Fresh-thread replay produces hash-equal pull outputs and materialized file. |\\n| TC-5.3 | `test/lifecycle.test.ts :: teardown continuity` | Fresh SDK between phase groups yields final pull, health, and materialized file equal to uninterrupted run. |\\n| TC-5.4 | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts :: checkpoint parity` | Spawned CLI overview/view/list reads at checkpoints deep-equal in-process SDK results. |\\n\\n#### Architecture-Risk Tests\\n\\n| Risk | Test File / Check | Test Description | Why AC/TC Mapping Alone Would Miss It |\\n|------|-------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------|\\n| Cross-epic lifecycle order drift | `test/lifecycle.test.ts` named-phase checkpoints | Run create, intake, drain, status, compact, pull, inspect, mutate, rebuild, compact, pull, materialize in order. | Individual story tests cannot catch ordering mismatches between surfaces. |\\n| Persistence relies on memory | `test/lifecycle.test.ts` fresh-SDK hook | Recreate SDK between phase groups and compare final outputs. | In-process success can hide state stored only in runtime memory. |\\n| CLI production path drift | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` process checkpoint leg | Spawn real commands and compare JSON to SDK checkpoints. | SDK tests do not prove command registration, stdout, or argv mapping. |\\n\\n#### Technical Notes\\n\\n- `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts` owns the sequence and phase names; tests own assertions.\\n- The receipt-vs-health check compares the second compact receipt sweep section with the health snapshot taken immediately before compact.\\n- Quality review of deterministic-provider text remains outside this epic.\\n\\n#### Anti-Shim Requirements\\n\\n- Use the real SDK configuration with deterministic provider and zero network/real-provider calls.\\n- Use real fresh SDK construction for teardown continuity.\\n- Use spawned CLI commands for checkpoint parity; do not call CLI handlers directly.\\n\\n#### Production Path Proof\\n\\n- Entrypoint: SDK surfaces from Epics 01-04 and spawned `lhc` commands.\\n- Registration/default path: the helper drives public SDK operations; process leg drives registered CLI commands.\\n- Evidence: lifecycle default tests, teardown continuity, replay determinism, and process checkpoint parity.\\n\\n#### Verification\\n\\n- Targeted: `pnpm verify`\\n- Story gate: `pnpm verify`\\n- Epic/process gate: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`\\n\\n#### Spec Deviations\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### Definition of Done\\n<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n- The scripted lifecycle runs through one SDK configuration with deterministic provider only.\\n- Checkpoint assertions cover pull, health, compact receipt, rebuild, and materialized output.\\n- Replay on a fresh thread produces byte-identical pull outputs and materialized files.\\n- SDK teardown between phases produces the same final state as uninterrupted execution.\\n- Spawned CLI checkpoint reads match in-process SDK JSON.\\n- TC-5.1 through TC-5.4 pass with one primary owner in this story.\\n\",\"numLines\":133,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":133}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/004-quick-fix.stdout.log:60:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":2,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"\\\"}\"}},\"session_id\":\"ceae9c6b-d571-491c-ba4d-0d8e5cb3a7be\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"0514d40d-c8e6-46cf-b662-20c86820666e\"}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/004-quick-fix.stdout.log:61:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_0191ipq9fMmCCmVf2FqL3Z4G\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01LNKy5TE9aw7rjnkNWGVgAW\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.ts\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":6418,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":18683,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":6418},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"ceae9c6b-d571-491c-ba4d-0d8e5cb3a7be\",\"uuid\":\"d066dad4-002e-417f-87dd-230be0ea5e6b\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CbycNPePWxEVQNn77Gr84\"}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/004-quick-fix.stdout.log:62:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":2},\"session_id\":\"ceae9c6b-d571-491c-ba4d-0d8e5cb3a7be\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"59d6aeef-edb8-4823-8abc-4215b404ecca\"}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/004-quick-fix.stdout.log:63:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"message_delta\",\"delta\":{\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null},\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":6418,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":18683,\"output_tokens\":242,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"thinking_tokens\":0},\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":2,\"output_tokens\":242,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":18683,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":6418,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":6418},\"type\":\"message\"}]},\"context_management\":{\"applied_edits\":[]}},\"session_id\":\"ceae9c6b-d571-491c-ba4d-0d8e5cb3a7be\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"b10a7dd1-f100-4b40-a385-300b446a7e3c\"}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/004-quick-fix.stdout.log:64:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01LNKy5TE9aw7rjnkNWGVgAW\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t// Story 4 (Epic 04), default suite: TC-5.1–5.3 — the full-surface lifecycle\\n2\\t// exercise. One scripted sequence (test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts) drives every\\n3\\t// built v1 surface in PI-extension call order against one real SDK\\n4\\t// configuration with the registry's deterministic provider: zero network and\\n5\\t// zero real-provider calls are structural (no other provider exists in the\\n6\\t// configuration), and every checkpoint assertion lives here, not in the\\n7\\t// script, so the replay (TC-5.2), teardown (TC-5.3), and process (TC-5.4,\\n8\\t// cli-process-inspect.test.ts) legs replay the same sequence.\\n9\\t//\\n10\\t// Determinism control: the wall clock is the one ambient input the built\\n11\\t// surfaces stamp into outputs (event recorded_at, view created_at, mutation\\n12\\t// timestamps), so this file freezes Date — and only Date; the scheduler's\\n13\\t// real setImmediate/setTimeout stay live for the background drains. With\\n14\\t// the clock frozen, pull outputs are byte-identical across runs with no\\n15\\t// normalization at all.\\n16\\t//\\n17\\t// One pinned deviation (AC-5.3/AC-5.4 file equality): a thread's id is the\\n18\\t// design's ONE random value (threads design decision 7), and the PI session\\n19\\t// header embeds it (`id: \\\"<threadId>:<timestamp>\\\"`). Two real threads cannot\\n20\\t// share an id through the public surface, so the materialized-file equality\\n21\\t// here substitutes each run's own thread id with a fixed placeholder and\\n22\\t// requires every other byte identical. Nothing else is normalized.\\n23\\timport { createHash } from \\\"node:crypto\\\";\\n24\\timport { readFileSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\n25\\timport { afterAll, beforeAll, describe, expect, it, vi } from \\\"vitest\\\";\\n26\\timport {\\n27\\t  estimateTokens,\\n28\\t  type FormReportEntry,\\n29\\t  type HealthReport,\\n30\\t  type MutationResult,\\n31\\t  type OpResult,\\n32\\t  type PullResult,\\n33\\t  type SweepReceipt,\\n34\\t  type ViewMessage,\\n35\\t} from \\\"../src/index.js\\\";\\n36\\timport {\\n37\\t  DELETED_MESSAGE_TEXT,\\n38\\t  EDITED_MESSAGE_TEXT,\\n39\\t  LIFECYCLE_PROFILE,\\n40\\t  runLifecycle,\\n41\\t  tempStore,\\n42\\t  type LifecycleRun,\\n43\\t  type TempStore,\\n44\\t} from \\\"./fixtures/index.js\\\";\\n45\\t\\n46\\tlet store: TempStore;\\n47\\tlet run: LifecycleRun;\\n48\\t\\n49\\tbeforeAll(async () => {\\n50\\t  vi.useFakeTimers({ toFake: [\\\"Date\\\"] });\\n51\\t  vi.setSystemTime(new Date(\\\"2026-06-12T00:00:00.000Z\\\"));\\n52\\t  store = tempStore();\\n53\\t  run = await runLifecycle(store, { name: \\\"baseline\\\" });\\n54\\t}, 60000);\\n55\\tafterAll(() => {\\n56\\t  vi.useRealTimers();\\n57\\t  store.cleanup();\\n58\\t});\\n59\\t\\n60\\tfunction ok<T>(result: OpResult<T>): T {\\n61\\t  if (!result.ok) {\\n62\\t    throw new Error(`expected ok result: ${JSON.stringify(result.error)}`);\\n63\\t  }\\n64\\t  return result.value;\\n65\\t}\\n66\\t\\n67\\tfunction sha256(value: string): string {\\n68\\t  return createHash(\\\"sha256\\\").update(value).digest(\\\"hex\\\");\\n69\\t}\\n70\\t\\n71\\tfunction measured(messages: readonly ViewMessage[]): number {\\n72\\t  return messages.reduce((sum, message) => sum + estimateTokens(message.content), 0);\\n73\\t}\\n74\\t\\n75\\tfunction clearedKeys(...mutations: MutationResult[]): string[] {\\n76\\t  return mutations\\n77\\t    .flatMap((mutation) => mutation.cleared)\\n78\\t    .map((target) => `${target.subjectKind}:${target.subjectId}:${target.form}`)\\n79\\t    .sort();\\n80\\t}\\n81\\t\\n82\\tfunction pendingKeys(...reports: Array<readonly FormReportEntry[]>): string[] {\\n83\\t  return reports\\n84\\t    .flat()\\n85\\t    .filter((entry) => entry.state === \\\"pending\\\")\\n86\\t    .map((entry) => `${entry.subjectKind}:${entry.subjectId}:${entry.form}`)\\n87\\t    .sort();\\n88\\t}\\n89\\t\\n90\\ttype SweepLine = SweepReceipt[\\\"owners\\\"][number];\\n91\\tfunction byOwnerKind(rows: readonly SweepLine[]): SweepLine[] {\\n92\\t  return [...rows].sort((a, b) =>\\n93\\t    `${a.owner}/${a.kind}`.localeCompare(`${b.owner}/${b.kind}`),\\n94\\t  );\\n95\\t}\\n96\\t\\n97\\t// The materialized file with the run's own thread id substituted — the one\\n98\\t// sanctioned normalization (see header).\\n99\\tfunction comparableSessionFile(lifecycleRun: LifecycleRun): string {\\n100\\t  return readFileSync(lifecycleRun.outPath, \\\"utf8\\\").replaceAll(\\n101\\t    lifecycleRun.threadId,\\n102\\t    \\\"<thread-id>\\\",\\n103\\t  );\\n104\\t}\\n105\\t\\n106\\tdescribe(\\\"TC-5.1 / AC-5.1: the full sequence completes ok through one SDK configuration\\\", () => {\\n107\\t  it(\\\"every phase operation returns ok with the deterministic provider only\\\", () => {\\n108\\t    const { phases } = run;\\n109\\t    expect(phases.create.ok).toBe(true);\\n110\\t    for (const batch of phases.intake) expect(batch.ok).toBe(true);\\n111\\t    expect(phases.drain.settled).toBe(true);\\n112\\t    expect(phases.status.ok).toBe(true);\\n113\\t    expect(phases.compact1.ok).toBe(true);\\n114\\t    expect(phases.pull1.ok).toBe(true);\\n115\\t    expect(phases.inspect1.overview.ok).toBe(true);\\n116\\t    expect(phases.inspect1.view.ok).toBe(true);\\n117\\t    expect(phases.inspect1.health.ok).toBe(true);\\n118\\t    expect(phases.mutate.edit.ok).toBe(true);\\n119\\t    expect(phases.mutate.delete.ok).toBe(true);\\n120\\t    expect(phases.mutate.healthAfterMutate.ok).toBe(true);\\n121\\t    expect(phases.rebuild.settled).toBe(true);\\n122\\t    expect(phases.health2.ok).toBe(true);\\n123\\t    expect(phases.compact2.ok).toBe(true);\\n124\\t    expect(phases.pull2.ok).toBe(true);\\n125\\t    expect(phases.materialize.ok).toBe(true);\\n126\\t  });\\n127\\t\\n128\\t  it(\\\"status recommends the compact the sequence performs next, with derivation settled\\\", () => {\\n129\\t    const status = ok(run.phases.status);\\n130\\t    expect(status.threshold).toBe(300);\\n131\\t    expect(status.tailTokens).toBeGreaterThan(status.threshold);\\n132\\t    expect(status.compactRecommended).toBe(true);\\n133\\t    expect(status.derivation).toEqual({ pending: 0, retrying: 0, failed: 0, blocked: 0 });\\n134\\t    expect(status.view).toBeNull(); // not yet compacted at this checkpoint\\n135\\t  });\\n136\\t});\\n137\\t\\n138\\tdescribe(\\\"TC-5.1 / AC-5.2: checkpoint coherence across the sequence\\\", () => {\\n139\\t  it(\\\"post-compact pull serves bands + tail, and the view report's loadCost prices that pull\\\", () => {\\n140\\t    const receipt = ok(run.phases.compact1);\\n141\\t    expect(receipt.profile).toBe(LIFECYCLE_PROFILE.name);\\n142\\t    const pull = ok(run.phases.pull1);\\n143\\t\\n144\\t    // Bands open the array in gradient order; the tail follows in record\\n145\\t    // order — the served shape the PI extension will consume.\\n146\\t    const bands = pull.messages.filter((message) => message.band !== undefined);\\n147\\t    expect(bands.map((message) => message.band)).toEqual([\\\"brief\\\", \\\"detailed\\\", \\\"smooth\\\"]);\\n148\\t    expect(pull.messages.slice(0, bands.length)).toEqual(bands);\\n149\\t    const tail = pull.messages.slice(bands.length);\\n150\\t    expect(tail.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n151\\t    expect(tail.every((message) => message.band === undefined)).toBe(true);\\n152\\t    expect(pull.meta.viewId).toBe(receipt.viewId);\\n153\\t    expect(pull.meta.compactPoint).toBe(receipt.compactPoint);\\n154\\t\\n155\\t    // Cross-epic loadCost checkpoint (test plan: report at compact1 vs\\n156\\t    // pull1): the inspect report's serving cost equals this independent\\n157\\t    // pull re-measured with the shared estimator.\\n158\\t    const report = ok(run.phases.inspect1.view);\\n159\\t    expect(report.meta?.viewId).toBe(receipt.viewId);\\n160\\t    expect(report.meta?.profile).toBe(LIFECYCLE_PROFILE.name);\\n161\\t    expect(report.loadCost.bandTokens).toBe(measured(bands));\\n162\\t    expect(report.loadCost.tailTokens).toBe(measured(tail));\\n163\\t    expect(report.loadCost.total).toBe(measured(pull.messages));\\n164\\t\\n165\\t    // Overview agrees on the same view identity with derivation settled.\\n166\\t    const overview = ok(run.phases.inspect1.overview);\\n167\\t    expect(overview.view?.viewId).toBe(receipt.viewId);\\n168\\t    expect(overview.derivation.pending).toBe(0);\\n169\\t    expect(overview.messages.deleted).toBe(0);\\n170\\t  });\\n171\\t\\n172\\t  it(\\\"post-mutation health shows exactly the cleared set pending; post-drain health shows it ready\\\", () => {\\n173\\t    const { mutate } = run.phases;\\n174\\t    const edit = ok(mutate.edit);\\n175\\t    const deleted = ok(mutate.delete);\\n176\\t    expect(edit.superseded).toEqual([]);\\n177\\t    expect(deleted.superseded).toEqual([]);\\n178\\t    // The deleted assistant_text owns no derived forms: its cascade clears\\n179\\t    // sibling turn forms only.\\n180\\t    expect(deleted.dropped).toEqual([]);\\n181\\t\\n182\\t    // The cascade contracts' cleared union IS the pending set the owners\\n183\\t    // report — no more, no less (AC-5.2's \\\"the cleared set pending\\\").\\n184\\t    const cleared = clearedKeys(edit, deleted);\\n185\\t    expect(cleared.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n186\\t    const pending = pendingKeys(ok(mutate.messagesNotReady), ok(mutate.turnsNotReady));\\n187\\t    expect(pending).toEqual(cleared);\\n188\\t\\n189\\t    // Health joins the same truth: pending counts sum to the cleared set,\\n190\\t    // with the queued replacement work live and unclaimed (the background\\n191\\t    // drain has not started — the snapshot precedes its first pass).\\n192\\t    const health = ok(mutate.healthAfterMutate);\\n193\\t    const pendingTotal = health.owners.reduce(\\n194\\t      (sum, row) => sum + row.counts.pending + row.counts.retrying,\\n195\\t      0,\\n196\\t    );\\n197\\t    expect(pendingTotal).toBe(cleared.length);\\n198\\t    // Queue visibility is counted per report entry (AC-4.5's by-construction\\n199\\t    // consistency), so queued equals the pending entries — all unclaimed.\\n200\\t    expect(health.queue).toEqual({ queued: cleared.length, claimed: 0 });\\n201\\t    expect(edit.queued.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n202\\t    expect(deleted.queued.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n203\\t    expect(health.failures).toEqual([]);\\n204\\t\\n205\\t    // Post-drain (rebuild settled): everything ready, nothing failed,\\n206\\t    // queue empty.\\n207\\t    const after = ok(run.phases.health2);\\n208\\t    for (const row of after.owners) {\\n209\\t      expect(row.counts.pending).toBe(0);\\n210\\t      expect(row.counts.retrying).toBe(0);\\n211\\t      expect(row.counts.failed).toBe(0);\\n212\\t      expect(row.counts.blocked).toBe(0);\\n213\\t      expect(row.counts.ready).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n214\\t    }\\n215\\t    expect(after.failures).toEqual([]);\\n216\\t    expect(after.repairPreview).toEqual([]);\\n217\\t    expect(after.queue).toEqual({ queued: 0, claimed: 0 });\\n218\\t  });\\n219\\t\\n220\\t  it(\\\"the second compact's view reflects post-edit content\\\", () => {\\n221\\t    const pull1 = ok(run.phases.pull1);\\n222\\t    const pull2 = ok(run.phases.pull2);\\n223\\t\\n224\\t    // Before the mutations: the original prompt and the to-be-deleted text\\n225\\t    // are served verbatim in the tail (full fidelity).\\n226\\t    expect(\\n227\\t      pull1.messages.some((m) => m.content === \\\"turn 12: please investigate area 12\\\"),\\n228\\t    ).toBe(true);\\n229\\t    expect(pull1.messages.some((m) => m.content === DELETED_MESSAGE_TEXT)).toBe(true);\\n230\\t\\n231\\t    // After mutate + rebuild + compact2: the edited prompt serves verbatim,\\n232\\t    // the deleted message is gone from the served view entirely.\\n233\\t    expect(\\n234\\t      pull2.messages.some(\\n235\\t        (m) => m.band === undefined && m.role === \\\"user\\\" && m.content === EDITED_MESSAGE_TEXT,\\n236\\t      ),\\n237\\t    ).toBe(true);\\n238\\t    expect(pull2.messages.some((m) => m.content.includes(DELETED_MESSAGE_TEXT))).toBe(false);\\n239\\t    expect(\\n240\\t      pull2.messages.some((m) => m.content === \\\"turn 12: please investigate area 12\\\"),\\n241\\t    ).toBe(false);\\n242\\t  });\\n243\\t\\n244\\t  it(\\\"the second compact receipt's sweep section agrees with the health report taken immediately before it\\\", () => {\\n245\\t    const receipt = ok(run.phases.compact2);\\n246\\t    const health: HealthReport = ok(run.phases.health2);\\n247\\t    expect(\\\"owners\\\" in receipt.sweep).toBe(true);\\n248\\t    const sweep = receipt.sweep as SweepReceipt;\\n249\\t\\n250\\t    // Field-level agreement per owner/kind: the sweep saw exactly the state\\n251\\t    // health reported — same ready counts, in-flight = pending + retrying,\\n252\\t    // and the failed/requeued/blocked sets empty on both sides.\\n253\\t    const expectedFromHealth = health.owners.map((row) => ({\\n254\\t      owner: row.owner,\\n255\\t      kind: row.kind,\\n256\\t      ready: row.counts.ready,\\n257\\t      inFlight: row.counts.pending + row.counts.retrying,\\n258\\t      requeued: [],\\n259\\t      blocked: [],\\n260\\t      permanentFailed: [],\\n261\\t    }));\\n262\\t    expect(byOwnerKind(sweep.owners)).toEqual(byOwnerKind(expectedFromHealth));\\n263\\t    expect(health.failures).toEqual([]);\\n264\\t  });\\n265\\t});\\n266\\t\\n267\\tdescribe(\\\"TC-5.2 / AC-5.3: replay determinism on a fresh thread\\\", () => {\\n268\\t  it(\\\"produces hash-equal pull outputs and a byte-identical materialized file (modulo the one random thread id)\\\", async () => {\\n269\\t    const replay = await runLifecycle(store, { name: \\\"replay\\\" });\\n270\\t\\n271\\t    // Pull outputs: exact hash equality, no normalization — the frozen\\n272\\t    // clock leaves no ambient input, so any inequality is real\\n273\\t    // nondeterminism in the built surfaces.\\n274\\t    const pulls: Array<[OpResult<PullResult>, OpResult<PullResult>]> = [\\n275\\t      [run.phases.pull1, replay.phases.pull1],\\n276\\t      [run.phases.pull2, replay.phases.pull2],\\n277\\t    ];\\n278\\t    for (const [original, replayed] of pulls) {\\n279\\t      expect(sha256(JSON.stringify(ok(replayed)))).toBe(sha256(JSON.stringify(ok(original))));\\n280\\t    }\\n281\\t\\n282\\t    // Materialized file: identical bytes after substituting each thread's\\n283\\t    // own id (the header's one random value — see file header note).\\n284\\t    expect(replay.threadId).not.toBe(run.threadId);\\n285\\t    expect(sha256(comparableSessionFile(replay))).toBe(sha256(comparableSessionFile(run)));\\n286\\t  }, 60000);\\n287\\t});\\n288\\t\\n289\\tdescribe(\\\"TC-5.3 / AC-5.4: teardown continuity — fresh createSdk between phase groups\\\", () => {\\n290\\t  it(\\\"yields final pull, health, and materialized file identical to the uninterrupted run's\\\", async () => {\\n291\\t    const teardown = await runLifecycle(store, {\\n292\\t      name: \\\"teardown\\\",\\n293\\t      freshSdkBetweenGroups: true,\\n294\\t    });\\n295\\t\\n296\\t    // No in-memory dependency: the end state lives in the thread file, so a\\n297\\t    // fresh instance continuing each phase group lands byte-identical.\\n298\\t    expect(JSON.stringify(ok(teardown.phases.pull2))).toBe(\\n299\\t      JSON.stringify(ok(run.phases.pull2)),\\n300\\t    );\\n301\\t    expect(ok(teardown.phases.health2)).toEqual(ok(run.phases.health2));\\n302\\t    expect(sha256(comparableSessionFile(teardown))).toBe(sha256(comparableSessionFile(run)));\\n303\\t  }, 60000);\\n304\\t});\\n305\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"ceae9c6b-d571-491c-ba4d-0d8e5cb3a7be\",\"uuid\":\"4d21aff9-40b3-4f85-9365-24f897a04426\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T15:34:43.536Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.ts\",\"content\":\"// Story 4 (Epic 04), default suite: TC-5.1–5.3 — the full-surface lifecycle\\n// exercise. One scripted sequence (test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts) drives every\\n// built v1 surface in PI-extension call order against one real SDK\\n// configuration with the registry's deterministic provider: zero network and\\n// zero real-provider calls are structural (no other provider exists in the\\n// configuration), and every checkpoint assertion lives here, not in the\\n// script, so the replay (TC-5.2), teardown (TC-5.3), and process (TC-5.4,\\n// cli-process-inspect.test.ts) legs replay the same sequence.\\n//\\n// Determinism control: the wall clock is the one ambient input the built\\n// surfaces stamp into outputs (event recorded_at, view created_at, mutation\\n// timestamps), so this file freezes Date — and only Date; the scheduler's\\n// real setImmediate/setTimeout stay live for the background drains. With\\n// the clock frozen, pull outputs are byte-identical across runs with no\\n// normalization at all.\\n//\\n// One pinned deviation (AC-5.3/AC-5.4 file equality): a thread's id is the\\n// design's ONE random value (threads design decision 7), and the PI session\\n// header embeds it (`id: \\\"<threadId>:<timestamp>\\\"`). Two real threads cannot\\n// share an id through the public surface, so the materialized-file equality\\n// here substitutes each run's own thread id with a fixed placeholder and\\n// requires every other byte identical. Nothing else is normalized.\\nimport { createHash } from \\\"node:crypto\\\";\\nimport { readFileSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\nimport { afterAll, beforeAll, describe, expect, it, vi } from \\\"vitest\\\";\\nimport {\\n  estimateTokens,\\n  type FormReportEntry,\\n  type HealthReport,\\n  type MutationResult,\\n  type OpResult,\\n  type PullResult,\\n  type SweepReceipt,\\n  type ViewMessage,\\n} from \\\"../src/index.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  DELETED_MESSAGE_TEXT,\\n  EDITED_MESSAGE_TEXT,\\n  LIFECYCLE_PROFILE,\\n  runLifecycle,\\n  tempStore,\\n  type LifecycleRun,\\n  type TempStore,\\n} from \\\"./fixtures/index.js\\\";\\n\\nlet store: TempStore;\\nlet run: LifecycleRun;\\n\\nbeforeAll(async () => {\\n  vi.useFakeTimers({ toFake: [\\\"Date\\\"] });\\n  vi.setSystemTime(new Date(\\\"2026-06-12T00:00:00.000Z\\\"));\\n  store = tempStore();\\n  run = await runLifecycle(store, { name: \\\"baseline\\\" });\\n}, 60000);\\nafterAll(() => {\\n  vi.useRealTimers();\\n  store.cleanup();\\n});\\n\\nfunction ok<T>(result: OpResult<T>): T {\\n  if (!result.ok) {\\n    throw new Error(`expected ok result: ${JSON.stringify(result.error)}`);\\n  }\\n  return result.value;\\n}\\n\\nfunction sha256(value: string): string {\\n  return createHash(\\\"sha256\\\").update(value).digest(\\\"hex\\\");\\n}\\n\\nfunction measured(messages: readonly ViewMessage[]): number {\\n  return messages.reduce((sum, message) => sum + estimateTokens(message.content), 0);\\n}\\n\\nfunction clearedKeys(...mutations: MutationResult[]): string[] {\\n  return mutations\\n    .flatMap((mutation) => mutation.cleared)\\n    .map((target) => `${target.subjectKind}:${target.subjectId}:${target.form}`)\\n    .sort();\\n}\\n\\nfunction pendingKeys(...reports: Array<readonly FormReportEntry[]>): string[] {\\n  return reports\\n    .flat()\\n    .filter((entry) => entry.state === \\\"pending\\\")\\n    .map((entry) => `${entry.subjectKind}:${entry.subjectId}:${entry.form}`)\\n    .sort();\\n}\\n\\ntype SweepLine = SweepReceipt[\\\"owners\\\"][number];\\nfunction byOwnerKind(rows: readonly SweepLine[]): SweepLine[] {\\n  return [...rows].sort((a, b) =>\\n    `${a.owner}/${a.kind}`.localeCompare(`${b.owner}/${b.kind}`),\\n  );\\n}\\n\\n// The materialized file with the run's own thread id substituted — the one\\n// sanctioned normalization (see header).\\nfunction comparableSessionFile(lifecycleRun: LifecycleRun): string {\\n  return readFileSync(lifecycleRun.outPath, \\\"utf8\\\").replaceAll(\\n    lifecycleRun.threadId,\\n    \\\"<thread-id>\\\",\\n  );\\n}\\n\\ndescribe(\\\"TC-5.1 / AC-5.1: the full sequence completes ok through one SDK configuration\\\", () => {\\n  it(\\\"every phase operation returns ok with the deterministic provider only\\\", () => {\\n    const { phases } = run;\\n    expect(phases.create.ok).toBe(true);\\n    for (const batch of phases.intake) expect(batch.ok).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.drain.settled).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.status.ok).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.compact1.ok).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.pull1.ok).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.inspect1.overview.ok).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.inspect1.view.ok).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.inspect1.health.ok).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.mutate.edit.ok).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.mutate.delete.ok).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.mutate.healthAfterMutate.ok).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.rebuild.settled).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.health2.ok).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.compact2.ok).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.pull2.ok).toBe(true);\\n    expect(phases.materialize.ok).toBe(true);\\n  });\\n\\n  it(\\\"status recommends the compact the sequence performs next, with derivation settled\\\", () => {\\n    const status = ok(run.phases.status);\\n    expect(status.threshold).toBe(300);\\n    expect(status.tailTokens).toBeGreaterThan(status.threshold);\\n    expect(status.compactRecommended).toBe(true);\\n    expect(status.derivation).toEqual({ pending: 0, retrying: 0, failed: 0, blocked: 0 });\\n    expect(status.view).toBeNull(); // not yet compacted at this checkpoint\\n  });\\n});\\n\\ndescribe(\\\"TC-5.1 / AC-5.2: checkpoint coherence across the sequence\\\", () => {\\n  it(\\\"post-compact pull serves bands + tail, and the view report's loadCost prices that pull\\\", () => {\\n    const receipt = ok(run.phases.compact1);\\n    expect(receipt.profile).toBe(LIFECYCLE_PROFILE.name);\\n    const pull = ok(run.phases.pull1);\\n\\n    // Bands open the array in gradient order; the tail follows in record\\n    // order — the served shape the PI extension will consume.\\n    const bands = pull.messages.filter((message) => message.band !== undefined);\\n    expect(bands.map((message) => message.band)).toEqual([\\\"brief\\\", \\\"detailed\\\", \\\"smooth\\\"]);\\n    expect(pull.messages.slice(0, bands.length)).toEqual(bands);\\n    const tail = pull.messages.slice(bands.length);\\n    expect(tail.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(tail.every((message) => message.band === undefined)).toBe(true);\\n    expect(pull.meta.viewId).toBe(receipt.viewId);\\n    expect(pull.meta.compactPoint).toBe(receipt.compactPoint);\\n\\n    // Cross-epic loadCost checkpoint (test plan: report at compact1 vs\\n    // pull1): the inspect report's serving cost equals this independent\\n    // pull re-measured with the shared estimator.\\n    const report = ok(run.phases.inspect1.view);\\n    expect(report.meta?.viewId).toBe(receipt.viewId);\\n    expect(report.meta?.profile).toBe(LIFECYCLE_PROFILE.name);\\n    expect(report.loadCost.bandTokens).toBe(measured(bands));\\n    expect(report.loadCost.tailTokens).toBe(measured(tail));\\n    expect(report.loadCost.total).toBe(measured(pull.messages));\\n\\n    // Overview agrees on the same view identity with derivation settled.\\n    const overview = ok(run.phases.inspect1.overview);\\n    expect(overview.view?.viewId).toBe(receipt.viewId);\\n    expect(overview.derivation.pending).toBe(0);\\n    expect(overview.messages.deleted).toBe(0);\\n  });\\n\\n  it(\\\"post-mutation health shows exactly the cleared set pending; post-drain health shows it ready\\\", () => {\\n    const { mutate } = run.phases;\\n    const edit = ok(mutate.edit);\\n    const deleted = ok(mutate.delete);\\n    expect(edit.superseded).toEqual([]);\\n    expect(deleted.superseded).toEqual([]);\\n    // The deleted assistant_text owns no derived forms: its cascade clears\\n    // sibling turn forms only.\\n    expect(deleted.dropped).toEqual([]);\\n\\n    // The cascade contracts' cleared union IS the pending set the owners\\n    // report — no more, no less (AC-5.2's \\\"the cleared set pending\\\").\\n    const cleared = clearedKeys(edit, deleted);\\n    expect(cleared.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    const pending = pendingKeys(ok(mutate.messagesNotReady), ok(mutate.turnsNotReady));\\n    expect(pending).toEqual(cleared);\\n\\n    // Health joins the same truth: pending counts sum to the cleared set,\\n    // with the queued replacement work live and unclaimed (the background\\n    // drain has not started — the snapshot precedes its first pass).\\n    const health = ok(mutate.healthAfterMutate);\\n    const pendingTotal = health.owners.reduce(\\n      (sum, row) => sum + row.counts.pending + row.counts.retrying,\\n      0,\\n    );\\n    expect(pendingTotal).toBe(cleared.length);\\n    // Queue visibility is counted per report entry (AC-4.5's by-construction\\n    // consistency), so queued equals the pending entries — all unclaimed.\\n    expect(health.queue).toEqual({ queued: cleared.length, claimed: 0 });\\n    expect(edit.queued.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(deleted.queued.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(health.failures).toEqual([]);\\n\\n    // Post-drain (rebuild settled): everything ready, nothing failed,\\n    // queue empty.\\n    const after = ok(run.phases.health2);\\n    for (const row of after.owners) {\\n      expect(row.counts.pending).toBe(0);\\n      expect(row.counts.retrying).toBe(0);\\n      expect(row.counts.failed).toBe(0);\\n      expect(row.counts.blocked).toBe(0);\\n      expect(row.counts.ready).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    }\\n    expect(after.failures).toEqual([]);\\n    expect(after.repairPreview).toEqual([]);\\n    expect(after.queue).toEqual({ queued: 0, claimed: 0 });\\n  });\\n\\n  it(\\\"the second compact's view reflects post-edit content\\\", () => {\\n    const pull1 = ok(run.phases.pull1);\\n    const pull2 = ok(run.phases.pull2);\\n\\n    // Before the mutations: the original prompt and the to-be-deleted text\\n    // are served verbatim in the tail (full fidelity).\\n    expect(\\n      pull1.messages.some((m) => m.content === \\\"turn 12: please investigate area 12\\\"),\\n    ).toBe(true);\\n    expect(pull1.messages.some((m) => m.content === DELETED_MESSAGE_TEXT)).toBe(true);\\n\\n    // After mutate + rebuild + compact2: the edited prompt serves verbatim,\\n    // the deleted message is gone from the served view entirely.\\n    expect(\\n      pull2.messages.some(\\n        (m) => m.band === undefined && m.role === \\\"user\\\" && m.content === EDITED_MESSAGE_TEXT,\\n      ),\\n    ).toBe(true);\\n    expect(pull2.messages.some((m) => m.content.includes(DELETED_MESSAGE_TEXT))).toBe(false);\\n    expect(\\n      pull2.messages.some((m) => m.content === \\\"turn 12: please investigate area 12\\\"),\\n    ).toBe(false);\\n  });\\n\\n  it(\\\"the second compact receipt's sweep section agrees with the health report taken immediately before it\\\", () => {\\n    const receipt = ok(run.phases.compact2);\\n    const health: HealthReport = ok(run.phases.health2);\\n    expect(\\\"owners\\\" in receipt.sweep).toBe(true);\\n    const sweep = receipt.sweep as SweepReceipt;\\n\\n    // Field-level agreement per owner/kind: the sweep saw exactly the state\\n    // health reported — same ready counts, in-flight = pending + retrying,\\n    // and the failed/requeued/blocked sets empty on both sides.\\n    const expectedFromHealth = health.owners.map((row) => ({\\n      owner: row.owner,\\n      kind: row.kind,\\n      ready: row.counts.ready,\\n      inFlight: row.counts.pending + row.counts.retrying,\\n      requeued: [],\\n      blocked: [],\\n      permanentFailed: [],\\n    }));\\n    expect(byOwnerKind(sweep.owners)).toEqual(byOwnerKind(expectedFromHealth));\\n    expect(health.failures).toEqual([]);\\n  });\\n});\\n\\ndescribe(\\\"TC-5.2 / AC-5.3: replay determinism on a fresh thread\\\", () => {\\n  it(\\\"produces hash-equal pull outputs and a byte-identical materialized file (modulo the one random thread id)\\\", async () => {\\n    const replay = await runLifecycle(store, { name: \\\"replay\\\" });\\n\\n    // Pull outputs: exact hash equality, no normalization — the frozen\\n    // clock leaves no ambient input, so any inequality is real\\n    // nondeterminism in the built surfaces.\\n    const pulls: Array<[OpResult<PullResult>, OpResult<PullResult>]> = [\\n      [run.phases.pull1, replay.phases.pull1],\\n      [run.phases.pull2, replay.phases.pull2],\\n    ];\\n    for (const [original, replayed] of pulls) {\\n      expect(sha256(JSON.stringify(ok(replayed)))).toBe(sha256(JSON.stringify(ok(original))));\\n    }\\n\\n    // Materialized file: identical bytes after substituting each thread's\\n    // own id (the header's one random value — see file header note).\\n    expect(replay.threadId).not.toBe(run.threadId);\\n    expect(sha256(comparableSessionFile(replay))).toBe(sha256(comparableSessionFile(run)));\\n  }, 60000);\\n});\\n\\ndescribe(\\\"TC-5.3 / AC-5.4: teardown continuity — fresh createSdk between phase groups\\\", () => {\\n  it(\\\"yields final pull, health, and materialized file identical to the uninterrupted run's\\\", async () => {\\n    const teardown = await runLifecycle(store, {\\n      name: \\\"teardown\\\",\\n      freshSdkBetweenGroups: true,\\n    });\\n\\n    // No in-memory dependency: the end state lives in the thread file, so a\\n    // fresh instance continuing each phase group lands byte-identical.\\n    expect(JSON.stringify(ok(teardown.phases.pull2))).toBe(\\n      JSON.stringify(ok(run.phases.pull2)),\\n    );\\n    expect(ok(teardown.phases.health2)).toEqual(ok(run.phases.health2));\\n    expect(sha256(comparableSessionFile(teardown))).toBe(sha256(comparableSessionFile(run)));\\n  }, 60000);\\n});\\n\",\"numLines\":305,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":305}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/004-quick-fix.stdout.log:65:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"message_stop\"},\"session_id\":\"ceae9c6b-d571-491c-ba4d-0d8e5cb3a7be\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"98041c9a-385c-4b03-8e5c-eefdd6af1c4b\"}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/004-quick-fix.stdout.log:66:{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"status\",\"status\":\"requesting\",\"uuid\":\"42a2f45f-2cce-485d-a5f4-f0952530f29c\",\"session_id\":\"ceae9c6b-d571-491c-ba4d-0d8e5cb3a7be\"}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/004-quick-fix.stdout.log:67:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"message_start\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_014ycamhNL61W7j5R177VGfz\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":10150,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":25101,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"epheme