{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"queue|listQueuedWork|queued|claimed|AC-4.5|TC-4.1\" docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md'","aggregated_output":"docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:13:| `test/inspect-health.test.ts` | default | TC-4.1–4.3 |\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:34:| TC-4.1 | inspect-health :: counts + queue consistency | mixed-state fixture: exact counts per owner/kind/state; queue section equals live-item counts from the same reports |\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:36:| TC-4.3 | inspect-health :: rebuild bracket | edit → health: cascade set pending with queued work visible (exact subjects per cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; disjoint forms untouched |\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:46:| Inspect quietly writes (work rows, boundary nudge, view touch) | **read-only delta assert**: shared helper snapshots observable state (queued work via owners, boundary/zone via status, view identity via describe, event/message counts) before/after *every* new operation; deep-equal after. Runs inside each TC file via wrapper | A single forgotten side effect makes \"inspect describes, never changes\" fiction; absence-of-delta is checkable, absence-of-write-code is not |\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:60:**Chunk 2 — inspect domain (S2).** Red: `inspect.*` stubs return not-implemented; fixture lacks mutation-variant (TC-4.3 unwritable → fixture work first). Green: `shared/inspect.ts` shapes; overview composition; health composition; `cli/inspect.ts`; delta-assert helper lands here and wraps Chunk 1's ops retroactively. TC-1.1–1.3, TC-4.1–4.3. ~11 tests.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:35:                                       .pull        .listQueuedWork\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:48:| `report(ref, {messageId?})` → `FormReportEntry[]` (queue join) | messages/turns (E02) | health, show |\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:49:| `listTurns` / `listChunks` / `listQueuedWork` | turns (E01/E02) | overview, health |\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:92:- **DD-2 (show composes report):** `show` = internal single-message read (same store read as `listMessages`, by id, full blocks) + `messages.report(ref, {messageId})` for the queue-joined forms. No new join machinery; `FormReportEntry` is the forms shape `show` returns.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:96:- **DD-6 (read-only, structurally tested):** the architecture-risk test snapshots observable state (work-item rows via `listQueuedWork`/reports, boundary position via `status`, view identity via `describe`, event/message counts) before and after every inspect/describe/show/list call and asserts deep equality. Read-only is asserted as absence-of-delta, not absence-of-write-code.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:145:`health(ref)`: `messages.report` + `turns.report` (full, not-ready included) + `listQueuedWork` both owners. Compose: counts by owner/kind/state from report entries' states; `failures[]` from `failed`/`blocked` entries (reason, attempts, lastError off `FormReportEntry`); `repairPreview[]` = failed-and-not-blocked subjects (reported, never requeued — AC-4.3); `queue` = queued/claimed counts from the live-item joins, consistent by construction with the same entries' states (AC-4.5). Rebuild visibility (AC-4.4) is two health calls bracketing a drain — no new mechanism, the cascade's pending states simply show.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:149:Scripted in `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`: phases named `create | intake | drain | status | compact1 | pull1 | inspect1 | mutate | rebuild | health2 | compact2 | pull2 | materialize`. Each phase returns its results to the driving test; checkpoint assertions live in the test, not the script. Teardown leg (TC-5.3) re-creates the SDK between named phase groups using the same script with a `freshSdk` hook. Receipt-vs-health cross-check (AC-5.2): `compact2`'s receipt sweep section against the `health2` snapshot taken immediately before — field-level equality on the failed/requeued sets.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:185:  queue: { queued: number; claimed: number };\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:11:**Objective:** Report thread composition, derivation state, repair preview, queue visibility, and rebuild visibility without changing state.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:15:**Scope Out:** Repair execution and mutations remain Feature 2 behavior. Inspect reports and previews; it never repairs, requeues, writes rows, transitions state, moves boundaries, derives forms, or invokes a provider.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:37:- **AC-4.2**: Failures carry actionable detail: subject id, form kind, reason, attempts, last error — enough to decide and target a requeue without raw SQL.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:39:- **AC-4.3**: The report previews repair: which forms a requeue pass would touch (failed and not blocked), reported and never executed.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:41:- **AC-4.4**: Rebuild visibility: after an edit or delete, health shows the cascade-cleared forms as pending with their queued work visible; after the queue drains, the same forms report ready. Two reads bracket a rebuild.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:43:- **AC-4.5**: Live queue visibility: queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail, consistent with the state counts in the same report.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:45:- **TC-4.1** (AC-4.1, AC-4.5): Fixture with manufactured mixed states (ready, failed-transient, failed-permanent, blocked, pending) → exact counts per owner, kind, and state; queue section consistent with pending counts.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:49:- **TC-4.3** (AC-4.4): Edit a mid-thread message → health shows the cascade's cleared set pending with queued work (exact subjects per the cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; nothing outside the cascade changed state.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:55:This story creates the inspect domain and its shared report shapes. `overview` composes list/status/describe reads into counts and summaries; `health` composes owner report surfaces and queue detail into state counts, failure detail, and repair preview.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:68:- Health must stay on owner report surfaces and queue detail.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:101:| TC-4.1 | `test/inspect-health.test.ts :: counts + queue consistency` | Mixed-state fixture returns exact counts per owner/kind/state and queue consistency. |\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:103:| TC-4.3 | `test/inspect-health.test.ts :: rebuild bracket` | Edit creates pending queued cascade set; after drain the same set is ready and disjoint forms are untouched. |\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:109:| Inspect writes while reporting | Shared read-only delta helper | Snapshot queued work, boundary/zone, view identity, and record counts before/after every new read. | Shape assertions do not prove absence of side effects. |\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:116:- Health reads owner reports and queued-work detail; `repairPreview` reports failed-not-blocked forms only.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:123:- Do not execute repair or requeue from `health`.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:145:- `inspect.health` composes owner report surfaces for counts, failures, repair preview, and queue visibility.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:148:- TC-1.1 through TC-1.3 and TC-4.1 through TC-4.3 pass with one primary owner in this story.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:6:**Depends on:** Epic 01 (record and read-back), Epic 02 (report/requeue surfaces, mutation cascade), Epic 03 (view storage, status, pull — in build; consumed as spec'd)\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:11:Read first: `../../01-onboard/02-domain-design.md` §Inspect (the domain's charter: read-only, reads through other domains' surfaces, never writes, repairs, or derives), §Messages (read ownership), §Thread view (the view state this epic reports on). The Epic 02 spec pack defines the report surfaces this epic composes (`messages.report`, `turns.report`, queue detail). The Epic 03 spec pack defines the view storage and status shapes the view-contents report reads.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:19:**Context:** the operator arrives with a question — what does this thread hold, what did the agent actually see, did the rebuild land, why is this view degraded — and acts on the answer with Feature 2's mutation and requeue operations. Inspect tells them where to point those.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:123:The state of every derived form, aggregated to act on. This is also where a mutation's rebuild is watched: cleared forms show pending with queued work, then land ready.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:128:- **AC-4.2**: Failures carry actionable detail: subject id, form kind, reason, attempts, last error — enough to decide and target a requeue without raw SQL.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:129:- **AC-4.3**: The report previews repair: which forms a requeue pass would touch (failed and not blocked), reported and never executed.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:130:- **AC-4.4**: Rebuild visibility: after an edit or delete, health shows the cascade-cleared forms as pending with their queued work visible; after the queue drains, the same forms report ready. Two reads bracket a rebuild.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:131:- **AC-4.5**: Live queue visibility: queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail, consistent with the state counts in the same report.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:135:- **TC-4.1** (AC-4.1, AC-4.5): Fixture with manufactured mixed states (ready, failed-transient, failed-permanent, blocked, pending) → exact counts per owner, kind, and state; queue section consistent with pending counts.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:137:- **TC-4.3** (AC-4.4): Edit a mid-thread message → health shows the cascade's cleared set pending with queued work (exact subjects per the cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; nothing outside the cascade changed state.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:170:**`HealthReport`**: owners[] (owner, kind, counts by state); failures[] (owner, subjectKind, subjectId, form, reason, attempts, lastError?); repairPreview[] (owner, subjectKind, subjectId, form); queue (queued, claimed).\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:181:- **No inference in this epic**: no Epic 04 operation invokes a provider; tests may use Epic 02 deterministic-provider setup (draining queued work through the fake) to prepare the derived states under test.\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:224:| AC-4.5 (derivation health) | Flow 4 (AC-4.1–4.3, 4.5) |\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:245:| AC-4.1 | TC-4.1 |\ndocs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:249:| AC-4.5 | TC-4.1 |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
