{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B6mF7iBuNxuD2EM5uiVEPr","type":"tool_result","content":"86:  boundaryPosition: number;\n134:  visibility: { zoneTokens: number; maxTokens: number };\n---story2 health queue---\n11:**Objective:** Report thread composition, derivation state, repair preview, queue visibility, and rebuild visibility without changing state.\n15:**Scope Out:** Repair execution and mutations remain Feature 2 behavior. Inspect reports and previews; it never repairs, requeues, writes rows, transitions state, moves boundaries, derives forms, or invokes a provider.\n37:- **AC-4.2**: Failures carry actionable detail: subject id, form kind, reason, attempts, last error — enough to decide and target a requeue without raw SQL.\n39:- **AC-4.3**: The report previews repair: which forms a requeue pass would touch (failed and not blocked), reported and never executed.\n41:- **AC-4.4**: Rebuild visibility: after an edit or delete, health shows the cascade-cleared forms as pending with their queued work visible; after the queue drains, the same forms report ready. Two reads bracket a rebuild.\n43:- **AC-4.5**: Live queue visibility: queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail, consistent with the state counts in the same report.\n45:- **TC-4.1** (AC-4.1, AC-4.5): Fixture with manufactured mixed states (ready, failed-transient, failed-permanent, blocked, pending) → exact counts per owner, kind, and state; queue section consistent with pending counts.\n49:- **TC-4.3** (AC-4.4): Edit a mid-thread message → health shows the cascade's cleared set pending with queued work (exact subjects per the cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; nothing outside the cascade changed state.\n55:This story creates the inspect domain and its shared report shapes. `overview` composes list/status/describe reads into counts and summaries; `health` composes owner report surfaces and queue detail into state counts, failure detail, and repair preview.\n68:- Health must stay on owner report surfaces and queue detail.\n101:| TC-4.1 | `test/inspect-health.test.ts :: counts + queue consistency` | Mixed-state fixture returns exact counts per owner/kind/state and queue consistency. |\n103:| TC-4.3 | `test/inspect-health.test.ts :: rebuild bracket` | Edit creates pending queued cascade set; after drain the same set is ready and disjoint forms are untouched. |\n109:| Inspect writes while reporting | Shared read-only delta helper | Snapshot queued work, boundary/zone, view identity, and record counts before/after every new read. | Shape assertions do not prove absence of side effects. |\n116:- Health reads owner reports and queued-work detail; `repairPreview` reports failed-not-blocked forms only.\n123:- Do not execute repair or requeue from `health`.\n145:- `inspect.health` composes owner report surfaces for counts, failures, repair preview, and queue visibility.\n---story2 boundary---","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43cf21d7-2126-46d9-a042-c8289cb3cd73","uuid":"912a44d9-27cd-4bd8-a66a-18b8a101c18c","timestamp":"2026-06-12T15:47:28.343Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"86:  boundaryPosition: number;\n134:  visibility: { zoneTokens: number; maxTokens: number };\n---story2 health queue---\n11:**Objective:** Report thread composition, derivation state, repair preview, queue visibility, and rebuild visibility without changing state.\n15:**Scope Out:** Repair execution and mutations remain Feature 2 behavior. Inspect reports and previews; it never repairs, requeues, writes rows, transitions state, moves boundaries, derives forms, or invokes a provider.\n37:- **AC-4.2**: Failures carry actionable detail: subject id, form kind, reason, attempts, last error — enough to decide and target a requeue without raw SQL.\n39:- **AC-4.3**: The report previews repair: which forms a requeue pass would touch (failed and not blocked), reported and never executed.\n41:- **AC-4.4**: Rebuild visibility: after an edit or delete, health shows the cascade-cleared forms as pending with their queued work visible; after the queue drains, the same forms report ready. Two reads bracket a rebuild.\n43:- **AC-4.5**: Live queue visibility: queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail, consistent with the state counts in the same report.\n45:- **TC-4.1** (AC-4.1, AC-4.5): Fixture with manufactured mixed states (ready, failed-transient, failed-permanent, blocked, pending) → exact counts per owner, kind, and state; queue section consistent with pending counts.\n49:- **TC-4.3** (AC-4.4): Edit a mid-thread message → health shows the cascade's cleared set pending with queued work (exact subjects per the cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; nothing outside the cascade changed state.\n55:This story creates the inspect domain and its shared report shapes. `overview` composes list/status/describe reads into counts and summaries; `health` composes owner report surfaces and queue detail into state counts, failure detail, and repair preview.\n68:- Health must stay on owner report surfaces and queue detail.\n101:| TC-4.1 | `test/inspect-health.test.ts :: counts + queue consistency` | Mixed-state fixture returns exact counts per owner/kind/state and queue consistency. |\n103:| TC-4.3 | `test/inspect-health.test.ts :: rebuild bracket` | Edit creates pending queued cascade set; after drain the same set is ready and disjoint forms are untouched. |\n109:| Inspect writes while reporting | Shared read-only delta helper | Snapshot queued work, boundary/zone, view identity, and record counts before/after every new read. | Shape assertions do not prove absence of side effects. |\n116:- Health reads owner reports and queued-work detail; `repairPreview` reports failed-not-blocked forms only.\n123:- Do not execute repair or requeue from `health`.\n145:- `inspect.health` composes owner report surfaces for counts, failures, repair preview, and queue visibility.\n--