{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts | sed -n '35,75p' && nl -ba docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md | sed -n '30,52p;140,148p' && nl -ba docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md | sed -n '126,132p;166,171p'\"","aggregated_output":"    35\t// the owning domain's handler (registered at SDK construction, DD-6).\n    36\texport const WORK_KIND_REGISTRY: Readonly<\n    37\t  Record<WorkKind, { owner: WorkOwner; sourceRefKey: \"messageId\" | \"turnId\" | \"chunkId\" }>\n    38\t> = {\n    39\t  prompt_smoothing: { owner: \"messages\", sourceRefKey: \"messageId\" },\n    40\t  tool_call_summary: { owner: \"messages\", sourceRefKey: \"messageId\" },\n    41\t  tool_result_summary: { owner: \"messages\", sourceRefKey: \"messageId\" },\n    42\t  turn_derivation: { owner: \"turns\", sourceRefKey: \"turnId\" },\n    43\t  chunk_summary_detailed: { owner: \"turns\", sourceRefKey: \"chunkId\" },\n    44\t  chunk_summary_brief: { owner: \"turns\", sourceRefKey: \"chunkId\" },\n    45\t};\n    46\t\n    47\texport interface WorkItemRecord {\n    48\t  workItemId: string;\n    49\t  owner: WorkOwner;\n    50\t  kind: WorkKind;\n    51\t  sourceRef: WorkSourceRef;\n    52\t  status: \"queued\"; // the only status written before a drain claims (Epic 02 Story 1)\n    53\t  queuedAt: string;\n    54\t}\n    55\t\n    56\t// The derived forms an enqueue is scheduling work toward; the owning domain\n    57\t// names them (the util stays meaning-blind). Stored in the row's payload so\n    58\t// the drain's terminal paths (retry exhaustion, blocked source) can land the\n    59\t// form's failed/blocked state without asking any domain what a kind means.\n    60\texport interface EnqueueFormTarget {\n    61\t  subjectKind: SubjectKind;\n    62\t  subjectId: string;\n    63\t  form: FormKind;\n    64\t}\n    65\t\n    66\texport interface WorkItemInput {\n    67\t  owner: WorkOwner;\n    68\t  kind: WorkKind;\n    69\t  sourceRef: WorkSourceRef;\n    70\t  sourceVersion?: number; // defaults to 1 — first version of a fresh source\n    71\t  forms?: readonly EnqueueFormTarget[]; // carried in payload for the drain's terminal paths\n    72\t}\n    73\t\n    74\tfunction sourceIdOf(sourceRef: WorkSourceRef): string {\n    75\t  if (\"messageId\" in sourceRef) return sourceRef.messageId;\n    30\t                        │     │         │  │           │\n    31\t        ┌───────────────┘     │         │  └───────┐   └────────┐\n    32\t        ▼                     ▼         ▼          ▼            ▼\n    33\t   threads.resolve      intake-stream  thread-view  messages.report\n    34\t   listThreads          .listEvents    .describe(NEW) turns.report\n    35\t                                       .pull        .listQueuedWork\n    36\t                        messages.listMessages(+opts)\n    37\t                        messages.show (NEW)          turns.listTurns/listChunks\n    38\t```\n    39\t\n    40\t`inspect` sits at the top of the domain graph: pure consumer, imports five surfaces, nothing imports it except `sdk.ts` and `cli/`. No cycles — unlike Epic 03's sanctioned intake→thread-view cycle, this addition is acyclic by construction. `check-boundaries` gains the domain with no exception entries.\n    41\t\n    42\t### External Contracts (consumed, as built)\n    43\t\n    44\t| Contract | Source | Used by |\n    45\t|----------|--------|---------|\n    46\t| `listEvents` → ordered `EventRecord[]` | intake-stream (E01) | overview (count, span) |\n    47\t| `listMessages` → `MessageRecord[]` with `forms?` attached | messages (E01 + E02 AC-4.7) | overview, list/show |\n    48\t| `report(ref, {messageId?})` → `FormReportEntry[]` (queue join) | messages/turns (E02) | health, show |\n    49\t| `listTurns` / `listChunks` / `listQueuedWork` | turns (E01/E02) | overview, health |\n    50\t| `status` → `ViewStatus` | thread-view (E03) | overview (visibility, derivation counts) |\n    51\t| `pull` → `PullResult` | thread-view (E03) | view (loadCost by construction) |\n    52\t| `thread_view` row + bands (storage, in-domain) | thread-view (E03) | `describe` only |\n   140\t\n   141\t`listMessages(ref, opts)`: existing read + WHERE bounds on `source_event_order`, LIMIT, deleted filter (default excluded; `includeDeleted` includes flagged). `show(ref, messageId)`: by-id read, full blocks verbatim from the record, `deleted` flag honest, forms from `report({messageId})`. Not-found → `message_not_found` (existing code). Deleted + show → `ok` with flagged record (AC-3.3: audit, never not-found).\n   142\t\n   143\t### Flow 4: Health\n   144\t\n   145\t`health(ref)`: `messages.report` + `turns.report` (full, not-ready included) + `listQueuedWork` both owners. Compose: counts by owner/kind/state from report entries' states; `failures[]` from `failed`/`blocked` entries (reason, attempts, lastError off `FormReportEntry`); `repairPreview[]` = failed-and-not-blocked subjects (reported, never requeued — AC-4.3); `queue` = queued/claimed counts from the live-item joins, consistent by construction with the same entries' states (AC-4.5). Rebuild visibility (AC-4.4) is two health calls bracketing a drain — no new mechanism, the cascade's pending states simply show.\n   146\t\n   147\t### Flow 5: Lifecycle Exercise\n   148\t\n   126\t\n   127\t- **AC-4.1**: `inspect.health` aggregates across owners — counts by owner, form kind, and state (ready, pending, retrying, failed, blocked) — assembled entirely from the owners' report surfaces, never from direct `derived_form` or `work_item` reads.\n   128\t- **AC-4.2**: Failures carry actionable detail: subject id, form kind, reason, attempts, last error — enough to decide and target a requeue without raw SQL.\n   129\t- **AC-4.3**: The report previews repair: which forms a requeue pass would touch (failed and not blocked), reported and never executed.\n   130\t- **AC-4.4**: Rebuild visibility: after an edit or delete, health shows the cascade-cleared forms as pending with their queued work visible; after the queue drains, the same forms report ready. Two reads bracket a rebuild.\n   131\t- **AC-4.5**: Live queue visibility: queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail, consistent with the state counts in the same report.\n   132\t\n   166\t**`ViewContentsReport`**: meta (viewId, createdAt, profile, config, compactPoint, coveredFrom) | null; bands — ordered entries (subjectKind, subjectId, formUsed, degraded) and stored tokens per band; gaps (band, subjectId, reason); tail (messageCount, tokens as served); loadCost (bandTokens, tailTokens, total — equals what pull serves); sourceState (provenance as stored).\n   167\t\n   168\t**`threadView.describe`**: the stored active view row exposed read-only — arrangement, gaps, config, source state, identity/timestamps. Absent view → ok with null (not an error). This is the one surface addition outside inspect; it exists so inspect never touches `thread_view` tables.\n   169\t\n   170\t**`HealthReport`**: owners[] (owner, kind, counts by state); failures[] (owner, subjectKind, subjectId, form, reason, attempts, lastError?); repairPreview[] (owner, subjectKind, subjectId, form); queue (queued, claimed).\n   171\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
