{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/shared/inspect.ts | sed -n '48,76p' && nl -ba src/domains/inspect/internal/view-report.ts | sed -n '60,84p' && nl -ba docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md | sed -n '94,98p;157,174p' && nl -ba docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md | sed -n '112,132p'\"","aggregated_output":"    48\t    config: { lowerBound: number; percentages: Record<string, number> };\n    49\t    compactPoint: number;\n    50\t    coveredFrom: number;\n    51\t  } | null;\n    52\t  bands: Array<{\n    53\t    band: Band;\n    54\t    entries: Array<{\n    55\t      subjectKind: \"chunk\" | \"turn\";\n    56\t      subjectId: string;\n    57\t      formUsed: string;\n    58\t      degraded: boolean;\n    59\t    }>;\n    60\t    storedTokens: number;\n    61\t  }>;\n    62\t  gaps: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\n    63\t  tail: { messageCount: number; tokens: number }; // as served (AC-2.2)\n    64\t  // loadCost totals what pull serves NOW (AC-2.3): band and tail tokens are\n    65\t  // both measured over pull's served messages with the shared estimator, so\n    66\t  // equality with an independent pull is structural. The stored per-band\n    67\t  // counts stay reported above (bands[].storedTokens, AC-2.1) — they price\n    68\t  // the snapshot bytes without the served band-marker header, so they are\n    69\t  // describe's truth, not the serving cost.\n    70\t  loadCost: { bandTokens: number; tailTokens: number; total: number }; // = pull (AC-2.3)\n    71\t  // Provenance verbatim (AC-2.5); null on a never-compacted thread — no\n    72\t  // compact ever recorded what it saw, and inventing zeros would fabricate\n    73\t  // provenance (AC-2.4's view-null shape extends here).\n    74\t  sourceState: { maxEventOrder: number; formCounts: Record<string, number> } | null;\n    75\t}\n    76\t\n    60\t              degraded: entry.degraded,\n    61\t            }));\n    62\t          const storedBand = stored.bands.find((row) => row.band === band);\n    63\t          if (entries.length === 0 && storedBand === undefined) return [];\n    64\t          return [{ band, entries, storedTokens: storedBand?.storedTokens ?? 0 }];\n    65\t        });\n    66\t\n    67\t  const bandTokens = measuredTokens(bandMessages);\n    68\t  const tailTokens = measuredTokens(tailMessages);\n    69\t\n    70\t  return {\n    71\t    ok: true,\n    72\t    value: {\n    73\t      meta:\n    74\t        stored === null\n    75\t          ? null\n    76\t          : {\n    77\t              viewId: stored.viewId,\n    78\t              createdAt: stored.createdAt,\n    79\t              profile: stored.profileName,\n    80\t              config: stored.config,\n    81\t              compactPoint: stored.compactPoint,\n    82\t              coveredFrom: stored.coveredFrom,\n    83\t            },\n    84\t      bands,\n    94\t- **DD-4 (loadCost by construction):** `view-report.ts` calls `describe` (stored bands: entries, gaps, config, stored token counts) and `pull` (served messages). `loadCost.bandTokens` = sum of stored band counts; `loadCost.tailTokens` = estimator over pull's tail messages (band-absent entries); `total` = sum. Pull is the single costing authority for the tail — AC-2.2's boundary-aware shortening is inherited, not re-implemented.\n    95\t- **DD-5 (overview's view section):** composed from `status` (boundary, zone, derivation counts, view health) + `describe` (viewId, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom) — both already exist; overview adds no view logic.\n    96\t- **DD-6 (read-only, structurally tested):** the architecture-risk test snapshots observable state (work-item rows via `listQueuedWork`/reports, boundary position via `status`, view identity via `describe`, event/message counts) before and after every inspect/describe/show/list call and asserts deep equality. Read-only is asserted as absence-of-delta, not absence-of-write-code.\n    97\t- **DD-7 (no migration):** schema terminal at v6. The one index temptation (message kind counts) is declined — counts come from list reads (Spec Validation #2); if profiling ever demands an index, that is a v7 proposal.\n    98\t- **DD-8 (suite placement):** TC-5.1–5.3 default suite; TC-5.4 process suite. The lifecycle script is a shared fixture helper (`test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`) both suites drive, so the spawned leg replays the same sequence rather than a re-described one.\n   157\t  thread: { id: string; createdAt: string; metadata?: Record<string, string> };\n   158\t  events: { count: number; span: { first: number; last: number } | null };\n   159\t  messages: { visible: number; byKind: Record<string, number>; deleted: number; visibleTokens: number };\n   160\t  turns: { open: number; closed: number };\n   161\t  chunks: { count: number; unchunkedTurns: number };\n   162\t  derivation: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number };\n   163\t  view: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\n   164\t  visibility: { boundaryPosition: number; zoneTokens: number };\n   165\t}\n   166\t\n   167\texport interface ViewContentsReport {\n   168\t  meta: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; profile: string | null;\n   169\t          config: { lowerBound: number; percentages: Record<string, number> };\n   170\t          compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\n   171\t  bands: Array<{ band: Band; entries: Array<{ subjectKind: \"chunk\" | \"turn\"; subjectId: string;\n   172\t          formUsed: string; degraded: boolean }>; storedTokens: number }>;\n   173\t  gaps: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\n   174\t  tail: { messageCount: number; tokens: number };          // as served (AC-2.2)\n   112\t\n   113\t#### Verification\n   114\t\n   115\t- Targeted: `pnpm verify`\n   116\t- Story gate: `pnpm verify`\n   117\t- Epic/process gate: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`\n   118\t\n   119\t#### Spec Deviations\n   120\t\n   121\tNone.\n   122\t\n   123\t### Definition of Done\n   124\t<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\n   125\t- `threadView.describe` exposes the stored active view row read-only and returns null when absent.\n   126\t- `inspect.view` reports stored bands, gaps, config, provenance, tail, and loadCost.\n   127\t- `loadCost.total` equals measured `pull` content for compacted and never-compacted threads.\n   128\t- `lhc inspect view` returns SDK-parity JSON.\n   129\t- TC-2.1 through TC-2.3 pass with one primary owner in this story.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
