{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/lifecycle.test.ts | sed -n '88,106p;268,302p' && nl -ba docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md | sed -n '148,158p' && nl -ba docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md | sed -n '36,40p'\"","aggregated_output":"    88\t}\n    89\t\n    90\ttype SweepLine = SweepReceipt[\"owners\"][number];\n    91\tfunction byOwnerKind(rows: readonly SweepLine[]): SweepLine[] {\n    92\t  return [...rows].sort((a, b) =>\n    93\t    `${a.owner}/${a.kind}`.localeCompare(`${b.owner}/${b.kind}`),\n    94\t  );\n    95\t}\n    96\t\n    97\t// The materialized file with the run's own thread id substituted — the one\n    98\t// sanctioned normalization (see header).\n    99\tfunction comparableSessionFile(lifecycleRun: LifecycleRun): string {\n   100\t  return readFileSync(lifecycleRun.outPath, \"utf8\").replaceAll(\n   101\t    lifecycleRun.threadId,\n   102\t    \"<thread-id>\",\n   103\t  );\n   104\t}\n   105\t\n   106\tdescribe(\"TC-5.1 / AC-5.1: the full sequence completes ok through one SDK configuration\", () => {\n   268\t  it(\"produces hash-equal pull outputs and a byte-identical materialized file (modulo the one random thread id)\", async () => {\n   269\t    const replay = await runLifecycle(store, { name: \"replay\" });\n   270\t\n   271\t    // Pull outputs: exact hash equality, no normalization — the frozen\n   272\t    // clock leaves no ambient input, so any inequality is real\n   273\t    // nondeterminism in the built surfaces.\n   274\t    const pulls: Array<[OpResult<PullResult>, OpResult<PullResult>]> = [\n   275\t      [run.phases.pull1, replay.phases.pull1],\n   276\t      [run.phases.pull2, replay.phases.pull2],\n   277\t    ];\n   278\t    for (const [original, replayed] of pulls) {\n   279\t      expect(sha256(JSON.stringify(ok(replayed)))).toBe(sha256(JSON.stringify(ok(original))));\n   280\t    }\n   281\t\n   282\t    // Materialized file: identical bytes after substituting each thread's\n   283\t    // own id (the header's one random value — see file header note).\n   284\t    expect(replay.threadId).not.toBe(run.threadId);\n   285\t    expect(sha256(comparableSessionFile(replay))).toBe(sha256(comparableSessionFile(run)));\n   286\t  }, 60000);\n   287\t});\n   288\t\n   289\tdescribe(\"TC-5.3 / AC-5.4: teardown continuity — fresh createSdk between phase groups\", () => {\n   290\t  it(\"yields final pull, health, and materialized file identical to the uninterrupted run's\", async () => {\n   291\t    const teardown = await runLifecycle(store, {\n   292\t      name: \"teardown\",\n   293\t      freshSdkBetweenGroups: true,\n   294\t    });\n   295\t\n   296\t    // No in-memory dependency: the end state lives in the thread file, so a\n   297\t    // fresh instance continuing each phase group lands byte-identical.\n   298\t    expect(JSON.stringify(ok(teardown.phases.pull2))).toBe(\n   299\t      JSON.stringify(ok(run.phases.pull2)),\n   300\t    );\n   301\t    expect(ok(teardown.phases.health2)).toEqual(ok(run.phases.health2));\n   302\t    expect(sha256(comparableSessionFile(teardown))).toBe(sha256(comparableSessionFile(run)));\n   148\t- **AC-5.2**: Checkpoint coherence: post-compact pull serves bands + tail; post-mutation health shows the cleared set pending; post-drain health shows it ready; the second compact's view reflects post-edit content; the second compact receipt's sweep section agrees with the health report taken immediately before it.\n   149\t- **AC-5.3**: End-to-end determinism: the whole sequence replayed on a fresh thread produces byte-identical pull outputs and materialized files.\n   150\t- **AC-5.4**: No in-memory dependency: tearing down the SDK instance between phases and continuing on a fresh `createSdk` yields the same end state as the uninterrupted run.\n   151\t- **AC-5.5**: Operator parity: inspect and view reads driven through the spawned CLI at checkpoints return the same JSON as the in-process SDK calls at those checkpoints.\n   152\t\n   153\t#### Test Conditions\n   154\t\n   155\t- **TC-5.1** (AC-5.1, AC-5.2): Scripted lifecycle with checkpoint assertions at each named step; receipt-vs-health cross-check exact.\n   156\t- **TC-5.2** (AC-5.3): Replay on a fresh thread → hash equality on every pull output and the materialized file.\n   157\t- **TC-5.3** (AC-5.4): Teardown and recreate the SDK between intake/compact/mutation phases → final pull, health, and materialized file identical to TC-5.1's.\n   158\t- **TC-5.4** (AC-5.5): Process-suite leg: spawned CLI inspect/view/messages reads at three checkpoints equal the in-process results.\n    36\t| TC-4.3 | inspect-health :: rebuild bracket | edit → health: cascade set pending with queued work visible (exact subjects per cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; disjoint forms untouched |\n    37\t| TC-5.1 | lifecycle :: full sequence + checkpoints | every phase ok; post-compact pull = bands+tail; mutate → pending; drain → ready; compact2 reflects edit; receipt sweep section field-equals pre-compact health snapshot |\n    38\t| TC-5.2 | lifecycle :: replay determinism | fresh thread, same script → hash-equal pull outputs and materialized file |\n    39\t| TC-5.3 | lifecycle :: teardown continuity | `freshSdk` between phase groups → final pull/health/file identical to TC-5.1 run |\n    40\t| TC-5.4 | cli-process-inspect :: checkpoint parity | spawned CLI overview/view/list at three checkpoints deep-equal in-process results at same checkpoints |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
