mId: item.workItemId,\n   515\t      owner: item.owner,\n   516\t      kind: item.kind,\n   517\t      sourceRef: item.sourceRef,\n   518\t      status: row.status as \"queued\" | \"claimed\",\n   519\t      attempts: item.attempts,\n   520\t      queuedAt: item.queuedAt,\n   521\t      sourceVersion: item.sourceVersion,\n   522\t    };\n   523\t    if (row.last_error !== null) detail.lastError = row.last_error;\n   524\t    if (row.eligible_at !== null) detail.eligibleAt = row.eligible_at;\n   525\t    if (row.claimed_at !== null) detail.claimedAt = row.claimed_at;\n   526\t    if (row.claim_expires_at !== null) detail.claimExpiresAt = row.claim_expires_at;\n   527\t    return detail;\n   528\t  });\n   529\t}\n   530\t\n   531\t// Listing in queue order (insertion order within the walk); each owning\n   532\t// domain lists only its own items.\n   533\texport function listItems(db: DatabaseSync, owner: WorkOwner): WorkItemRecord[] {\n   534\t  const rows = db\n   535\t    .prepare(\n   536\t      `SELECT work_item_id, owner, kind, source_ref, queued_at\n   537\t       FROM work_item WHERE owner = ? ORDER BY rowid`,\n   538\t    )\n   539\t    .all(owner) as unknown as RawWorkItemRow[];\n   540\t  return rows.map((row) => ({\n   541\t    workItemId: row.work_item_id,\n   542\t    owner: row.owner as WorkOwner,\n   543\t    kind: row.kind as WorkKind,\n   544\t    sourceRef: JSON.parse(row.source_ref) as WorkSourceRef,\n   545\t    status: \"queued\",\n   546\t    queuedAt: row.queued_at,\n   547\t  }));\n   548\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
