{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_66","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 1-4 are wired through the SDK and CLI and the configured gates pass: `pnpm verify` passed with 328 tests and `pnpm verify-all` passed with 366 tests / 44 files, including the process suite.\",\"Flow 4 has unresolved cross-story semantic drift: `inspect.health.queue` reports one queued/claimed count per pending form report entry, while the epic and tech design describe queued/claimed work counts from owner queue detail. A turn-derivation work item that owns two forms is counted twice by health.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"`domains/inspect/**` imports owner surfaces only; `check-boundaries` passed and the inspect source check found no raw SQL/table access in inspect.\",\"`inspect.view` and lifecycle determinism intentionally follow approved rulings, but the epic-level artifacts still contain older wording for materialized-file byte identity and the tech design still says `loadCost.bandTokens` is the stored band-count sum.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Most epic ACs have direct default/process suite coverage across `messages-read`, `inspect-overview`, `inspect-health`, `inspect-view`, `lifecycle`, and `cli-process-inspect`.\",\"AC-4.5 is not conclusively covered because the tests assert consistency with pending form-entry counts, not queue-detail work-item counts.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No material fake adapter, shim, placeholder, or non-real production execution path was found in the audited SDK/CLI inspect, message-read, thread-view, and lifecycle paths.\",\"Material production-path issue: `inspect.health` derives queue counts from `FormReportEntry.queue` per form entry and does not count live queue work rows; on a mutation-in-flight production fixture it returned `{queued:5, claimed:0}` while owner `listQueuedWork` surfaces showed four live work items.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-04-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Health queue counts do not match queue-detail work counts\",\"evidence\":\"Epic AC-4.5 requires queued and claimed work counts from owner queue detail; tech-design Flow 4 says `health` composes `messages.report` + `turns.report` + `listQueuedWork` both owners. In `src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-105`, `composeHealth` only reads `messages.report` and `turns.report`, then increments `queue` once for every report entry with `entry.queue` at lines 89-95. In an ad hoc mutation-in-flight fixture, `inspect.health` returned `healthQueue:{queued:5,claimed:0}` while `messages.listQueuedWork` + `turns.listQueuedWork` returned four work item ids: `w-m5-prompt_smoothing-v2`, `w-t2-turn_derivation-v2`, `w-c1-chunk_summary_brief-v2`, `w-c1-chunk_summary_detailed-v2`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-health.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.5\",\"TC-4.1\",\"tech-design Flow 4: Health\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-04-002\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Accepted deviation wording is not propagated through all epic-level artifacts\",\"evidence\":\"Story 4 and ruling-011 accept materialized-file equality after substituting only the random threadId, and tests implement that in `test/lifecycle.test.ts:97-103` and `:282-302`. The epic and test plan still say materialized files are byte-identical without that qualifier at `epic.md:149-157` and `test-plan.md:38-39`. Story 3/ruling-011 accepts measured pull-served `loadCost.bandTokens` and nullable `sourceState`, while `tech-design.md:94` still says `loadCost.bandTokens` is the sum of stored band counts and `stories/03-view-contents-report.md:119-121` still says no deviations.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"AC-2.5\",\"AC-5.3\",\"AC-5.4\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Decide whether `HealthReport.queue` is intended to count live work items or pending/retrying form entries. The current implementation and tests use form-entry counts; the epic/tech-design wording points to queue-detail work counts.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
