{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01GMwaJDqtUAoFUAebtwR8Si","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n  \"crossStoryFindings\": [\n    \"Story 2 → Story 3 handoff completed as tracked: overview's interim view-summary source (pull().meta, Story 2 approved deviation) was swapped to threadView.describe in Story 3 (overview.ts), and the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced with the real composeViewReport. The receipt-tracked risk is closed in code, not just in the log.\",\n    \"Shared vocabulary discipline holds across stories: report shapes live in src/shared/inspect.ts (Story 2) and Story 3 consumes them without redefinition; messages.show reuses the owner's reportMessageForms read (DD-2) rather than new join machinery; the lifecycle fixture (test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts) is one script driven by all four TC-5 legs including the process-suite leg (DD-8), so replay/teardown/CLI runs exercise the same sequence.\",\n    \"The read-only delta helper (test/fixtures/read-only-delta.ts, Story 2) wraps Story 1's ops retroactively as the test plan required: inspect-overview/view/health tests use expectReadOnly, messages-read uses the same observableState snapshot directly, and the Story 3 storedView field was added to the snapshot so a forgotten view touch is caught even when pull meta would not show it.\",\n    \"Cumulative baseline never regressed: 290 → 300 → 313 → 320 → 328 default tests across the four accepted stories; epic gate run for this review shows 366 tests / 44 files with the process suite included.\",\n    \"All four story receipts in team-impl-log.md show accepted status with verifier PASS, impl-lead-run gates, and disposition of every finding (SV-01-001..005, SV-03-001, SV-04-001); approved rulings (023 strict-read-purity, 011 Story 3 loadCost/sourceState, 011 Story 4 threadId-normalized file equality) are all reflected accurately in the shipped code.\"\n  ],\n  \"architectureFindings\": [\n    \"Composition discipline is structural, not aspirational: domains/inspect imports only the five other domains' index surfaces (verified in source), check-boundaries.mjs carries the inspect dependency allowlist plus the Epic 04 source check rejecting raw storage access from domains/inspect/** (scripts/check-boundaries.mjs:77-115), and the gate runs it. The domain graph addition is acyclic as designed.\",\n    \"Read-only is enforced at two layers as DD-6 demanded: every new operation (inspect.overview/view/health, threadView.describe, messages.listMessages/show) runs under runWithThreadTouchSuppressed so a background scheduler can never hang a catch-up drain off a read, and tests assert absence-of-delta over observable state including raw derived_form rows.\",\n    \"Minor drift from tech-design mechanics, surface-respecting in both cases: (1) DD-5 says overview takes boundary 'via status' but ViewStatus does not expose boundaryPosition — the implementation reads it from pull.meta (overview.ts:125-129, commented), which is the only surface exposing it; side effect is that every overview call performs a full pull render. (2) Tech design Flow 4 names listQueuedWork as a health input, but health.ts derives queue counts from the report entries' queue joins instead — consistent-by-construction with the same report's state counts, which is arguably stronger for AC-4.5, but the tech design was not updated to record either substitution.\",\n    \"Approved public-contract deviations are implemented exactly as ruled: loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages rather than stored sums (ruling-011 Story 3; AC-2.3's equality is the governing contract and the shared/inspect.ts comment documents why stored sums structurally cannot match), and sourceState/meta nullable for never-compacted threads.\",\n    \"Error model and CLI conventions inherited cleanly: one additive caller_error code (invalid_bounds, Story 1 approved ruling, Epic 03 precedent), no other additions; CLI commands are thin argv-to-SDK wrappers with semantic validation kept in the SDK so parity including refusals is structural (cli/inspect.ts, cli/messages-read.ts).\"\n  ],\n  \"epicCoverageAssessment\": [\n    \"All 23 ACs and 17 TCs are implemented and traceable: test describe blocks name their TC/AC pairs explicitly across inspect-overview.test.ts (TC-1.1–1.3), inspect-view.test.ts (TC-2.1–2.3 + describe purity legs), messages-read.test.ts (TC-3.1–3.3 + three architecture-risk suites), inspect-health.test.ts (TC-4.1–4.3 + provider-free leg), lifecycle.test.ts (TC-5.1–5.3 with all four AC-5.2 checkpoint assertions including the receipt-vs-health cross-check), and cli-process-inspect.test.ts (TC-3.4, TC-5.4, process suite).\",\n    \"AC-5.3/AC-5.4 materialized-file equality ships as threadId-normalized equality per approved Story 4 ruling-011: thread id is the design's one random value, the test substitutes only it and requires every other byte identical, with Date frozen so pull-output hash equality stays literal with zero normalization. The relaxation is principled, documented in the test header, and recorded in the story spec.\",\n    \"Zero-provider NFR is verified structurally for the whole epic: inspect/list/show/describe run green under a throwing provider, and the lifecycle's only provider is the registry's deterministic one (zero network, zero real-provider calls — AC-5.1).\",\n    \"Epic gate run by this reviewer: pnpm verify-all PASS, exit 0, 366/366 tests across 44 files with the process suite executed (LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 is baked into verify-all), build/typecheck/lint/boundaries all green.\",\n    \"Closeout items still owed per the epic's own assumptions: the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic must be recorded at closeout, and the search-deferral PRD/tech-arch backfill exists but is uncommitted (see unresolvedItems).\"\n  ],\n  \"productionPathFindings\": [\n    \"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholder execution paths remain on any production path. Grep for stub/placeholder/not-implemented across src/ finds only SQL parameter placeholders, comments, and the not_implemented code's vocabulary entry in shared/errors.ts — no operation returns it anymore; the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real implementation in Story 3.\",\n    \"Provider posture is honest by construction: the registry (src/providers/registry.ts) contains exactly one provider — deterministic — which is the spec'd v1 state (real inference is explicitly next-PRD scope, carried in the epic's Out of Scope). There is no default provider: the CLI resolves only an explicitly named provider (--provider/LHC_PROVIDER) and fails with provider_not_configured rather than silently substituting the deterministic one.\",\n    \"The lifecycle exercise runs the real production SDK (createSdk) in background mode through the production registry's deterministic provider and the real drainSettled awaitable — no test-only seams in the sequence itself; the one test-only control is freezing Date in the test file, which is outside the production path.\",\n    \"Stale comment, cosmetic only: src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still describes 'inspect view' as a not-implemented stub that 'Story 3 makes real' — Story 3 landed, the route is real, and the command is in the help text. The comment is now false; the code is correct.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockingFindings\": [],\n  \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E04-ER1-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"Epic-level docs still carry literal 'byte-identical' phrasing superseded by approved ruling-011 (threadId-normalized file equality)\",\n      \"evidence\": \"epic.md AC-5.3/TC-5.2 (lines 149, 156-157), test-plan.md TC-5.2 (line 38), and coverage.md line 48 state byte-identical materialized-file equality; Story 4 ruling-011 (approved, recorded in team-impl-log.md and stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md) relaxed file equality to substitute the one random thread id, with pull-output hash equality remaining literal. The impl log itself flags this for epic-review awareness. The shipped test (lifecycle.test.ts:17-22, 97-104) implements the ruled contract correctly; only the epic-level docs lag.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\n        \"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\",\n        \"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/coverage.md\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-5.3\", \"AC-5.4\", \"TC-5.2\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E04-ER1-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Tech design not backfilled for two surface-respecting mechanism substitutions (overview boundary via pull.meta; health queue via report join)\",\n      \"evidence\": \"tech-design.md DD-5 says overview takes boundary/zone 'via status', but ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) exposes no boundaryPosition — overview.ts:125-129 reads it from pull.meta, the only surface that exposes it, at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Tech-design Flow 4 and the System View name listQueuedWork as a health input, but health.ts derives queue counts from FormReportEntry queue joins (consistent-by-construction with the same report's state counts). Both substitutions stay on surfaces and satisfy their ACs; neither is recorded as a design deviation.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\n        \"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/overview.ts\",\n        \"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-1.1\", \"AC-4.5\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E04-ER1-003\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Stale stub-era comment on the 'inspect view' CLI route\",\n      \"evidence\": \"src/cli/index.ts:473-475 says the route is 'routed ahead of its story so the CLI mirrors the SDK surface: the stub returns the structured not-implemented result; Story 3 makes it real (and adds it to the help text)' — Story 3 landed; runInspectView is the real implementation and the command appears in the help text (line 72). Comment is false, code is correct.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedItems\": [\n    \"Uncommitted working-tree changes carry the sanctioned PRD AC-4.3 search-deferral backfill (packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md, 01-tech-arch.md) plus impl-log state bookkeeping — these are epic-mandated doc changes (epic.md Out of Scope: 'backfilled with this epic') and should be committed as part of epic closeout.\",\n    \"Epic closeout must record the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic explicitly (epic.md Assumptions: 'Closeout records this explicitly') — not yet written; this review is upstream of that closeout step.\"\n  ],\n  \"gateResult\": \"pass\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2150,"cache_read_input_tokens":105938,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2150},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43cf21d7-2126-46d9-a042-c8289cb3cd73","uuid":"a063e633-1b6d-4ba1-b5f2-e07476725a3e","request_id":"req_011CbydQPiGuuWy8rUNFjCr7"}
